-- title:
--   Relations among degree-m forms spanning S_m are generated in degrees ≤ 1
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field, let $n, m, g$ be natural numbers, and let $S = K[x_0,\dots,x_n]$ be the polynomial ring in $n+1$ variables, realised as `MvPolynomial (Fin (n + 1)) K`. Let $F : \mathrm{Fin}\,g \to S$ be a family of polynomials such that each $F_i$ is homogeneous of degree $m$ (in the sense of `MvPolynomial.IsHomogeneous`: every monomial occurring in $F_i$ has total degree $m$, the zero polynomial being homogeneous of every degree), and assume that every $w \in S$ which is homogeneous of degree $m$ lies in the $K$-linear span of the set of values $F_i$, so that the $F_i$ span the space $S_m$ of degree-$m$ forms over $K$. Let $d$ be a natural number and let $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,g \to S$ be a family with each $c_i$ homogeneous of degree $d$ and $\sum_i c_i F_i = 0$. Then, as an element of $S^g$, the tuple $c$ lies in the $S$-submodule generated by the set of tuples $l : \mathrm{Fin}\,g \to S$ for which there is some $d' \le 1$ with every $l_i$ homogeneous of degree $d'$ and $\sum_i l_i F_i = 0$; that is, $c$ is an $S$-linear combination of relations whose entries are all constant or all linear.
--
--   This is the first-syzygy (linear presentation) statement for the $m$-th power of the irrelevant maximal ideal: since a family of degree-$m$ forms spanning $S_m$ generates $(x_0,\dots,x_n)^m$, its module of relations is generated by relations of degree $0$ and $1$, the constant relations recording linear dependencies among the $F_i$ together with the linear exchange relations; it is the degree-$1$ part of the classical fact that $(x_0,\dots,x_n)^m$ has an $m$-linear free resolution. It is used in the proof of [`MvPolynomial.exists_forall_eval_ne_zero_mem_of_mul_mem_of_finrank_piece_succ_eq_macaulayPow`](thm.html#MvPolynomial.exists_forall_eval_ne_zero_mem_of_mul_mem_of_finrank_piece_succ_eq_macaulayPow), and its own proof cites only the description of the relations among the variables $x_j$ themselves given by [`MvPolynomial.exists_skew_eq_sum_mul_X_of_sum_mul_X_eq_zero`](thm.html#MvPolynomial.exists_skew_eq_sum_mul_X_of_sum_mul_X_eq_zero) (every relation $\sum_j c_j x_j = 0$ comes from a skew-symmetric matrix).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_MvPolynomial_relation_mem_span_of_forall_isHomogeneous_mem_span.lean

